parabolic cylinder $4(x-3)^{2}=12(z+1)$ and the plane $y=2$ onto the $xz$-plane is a parabola. What is the vertex of the parabola?" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378382 1113 #uuid "53a8baa3-c5ca-5f72-a258-e1c548f3d50d" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378382 1145 "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $y=2,$ we substitute $y=2$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $y$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-3)^{2} & =12(z+1) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =3(z+1) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (z+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a parabola in the $xz$-plane with the vertex at $(3,-1).$" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378384 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378385 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378386 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378387 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378388 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1041 "selection" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378386 13194139535988 true] [17592186378383 1110 #uuid "88284024-50ea-548d-b12b-2b59a7c3b34f" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378384 1034 "(3,2)" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535988 true] [17592186378384 1111 #uuid "5041b9ec-f7ee-56be-a361-3f9f31cceb46" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378385 1034 "(-3,1)" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535988 true] [17592186378385 1111 #uuid "c3270b61-2113-5c94-81db-338949b60a97" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378386 1034 "(3,-1)" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535988 true] [17592186378386 1111 #uuid "67a1dfb3-bf99-586d-bddc-d9a8529b844d" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378387 1034 "(2,-1)" 13194139535988 true] [17592186378387 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604